# Accessibility & Screen Reader Compatibility (SPOTS)

All UI code the agent writes or modifies must be **fully accessible** and **screen reader compatible**. SPOTS serves children, teens, and caregivers in a healthcare context — inaccessible UI blocks real users from reporting symptoms and using critical flows.

**Target:** WCAG 2.1 Level AA (project baseline; see `app/_lib/testing/a11y.ts` and `.github/workflows/a11y.yml`).

## Non-negotiables

- **Semantic HTML first** — use native elements (`button`, `a`, `input`, `label`, `nav`, `main`, `header`, `footer`) before ARIA or custom widgets.
- **Keyboard complete** — every interactive control reachable and operable via keyboard; visible focus; logical tab order; no keyboard traps (except intentional modals with escape/close).
- **Screen reader meaningful** — every control has an accessible name; state changes are announced; decorative content is hidden from AT.
- **Do not ship color-only affordances** — pair with text or another non-color cue. Icon-only controls are OK when they have a clear `aria-label` (or visible text elsewhere).
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`** when adding animation (see existing patterns in the codebase).

## Semantic structure

- One `<h1>` per page/view; logical heading hierarchy (`h2` → `h3`, no skips).
- Main landmark: `#main-content` (see `app/_lib/utils/focus-a11y.ts`); skip link pattern in layout tests.
- Use lists, landmarks, and articles where content is grouped — avoid div-only layouts for navigable regions.

## Labels, names, and ARIA

- **Every** `input`, `select`, `textarea`, and custom control has a visible `<label>` or `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`.
- **Images:** meaningful `alt`; decorative images `alt=""` and/or `aria-hidden="true"`.
- **Icon-only buttons:** `aria-label` (e.g. close, delete, scroll).
- **Toggle/selection:** use `aria-pressed`, `aria-checked`, or `role="radiogroup"` + `aria-checked` as appropriate — follow `SelectableCard`, `HairStyleSelector`, `ProblemStationStyleRow`.
- **Dialogs/overlays:** `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, labelled (`aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`); trap focus inside; restore focus on close; background `inert` via `setMobileOverlayBackgroundInert` / overlay helpers in `app/_lib/utils/focus-a11y.ts`.
- **Live regions:** loading, errors, and view changes use `aria-live` (`polite` or `assertive`) — see `useViewTitleAnnouncement`, skeleton `aria-busy` patterns.
- **Prefer visible text over redundant ARIA** — avoid duplicating labels in `aria-label` when visible text already names the control (see `useHeaderController` comment on `aria-describedby`).

## Keyboard & focus

- Reuse `app/_lib/hooks/a11y/useRadioGroupKeyboard.ts` for roving tabindex / arrow-key groups.
- On route or view enter, use `useFocusOnViewEnter` / `focusElementForAssistiveTech` (Safari/VoiceOver-safe).
- Modals/menus: focus first focusable on open; return focus to trigger on close (`getOverlayFirstFocusable`).
- Do not remove focus outlines without an equally visible replacement (`focus-visible` utilities).

## Forms & dynamic content

- Associate validation/errors with fields (`aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby` pointing at error text).
- Announce async results (save success/failure, empty states) without relying on color alone.
- Loading states: `aria-busy="true"` where content is replacing, not merely decorative skeletons.

## SPOTS-specific

- **Pediatric copy** in accessible names must stay age-appropriate (align with `healthcare-requirements.mdc`).
- **Symptom flows** (cart, PRO-CTCAE questions, body map, Problem Station): selected state, progress, and destructive actions (delete) must be named and keyboard-operable.
- **Parent/child contexts:** do not expose PHI in `aria-label` beyond what is already visible and appropriate for the role.

## When writing or changing components

1. Match patterns in existing a11y-tested components under `app/_components/**/__tests__/*.a11y.test.tsx`.
2. For new or changed UI, add or update an a11y test using `expectNoA11yViolations` from `app/_lib/testing/a11y.ts`.
3. Run / respect `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` — do not disable a11y rules without team approval.
4. Flag gaps the agent cannot fully verify (e.g. color contrast in JSDOM, complex gestures) and note manual VoiceOver/NVDA checks for reviewers.

## Anti-patterns (reject in solutions)

- `<div onClick>` without `role`, keyboard handler, and accessible name
- `tabIndex={0}` on non-interactive elements to fake buttons
- `aria-hidden="true"` on focusable or essential content
- Placeholder-only labels with no accessible name
- Auto-playing media without user control
- Removing "Skip to main" or main landmark id

